            "text": "The scene model contains four distinct remembered objects in each view. Identities the model treats as known: View A \u2014 upper: blue cross; right: yellow circle; lower: red triangle; left: green square. View B \u2014 upper: blue circle; right: red triangle; left: yellow square; lower: no identified color or shape. In both views the right location currently dominates selection and is also the most recoverable now, while all objects\u2019 recoverability is predicted to decline over one and two steps.\n\nControllability differs by view. In A, every command is predicted to shift next selection to the upper location (the blue cross), so changing the command cannot redirect attention to the other locations. If commanded, attention would move to the upper object, altering which object is available next but not preventing its recoverability from declining. In B, each command reliably directs next selection to a different named location (upper, right, lower, left), so the system can redirect attention to specific objects there; recoverability for those objects would nevertheless decrease over the forecasted steps.",
